{
  "raw": {
    "https://hrjobs.csuohio.edu/postings/27439": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Advanced Manufacturing)",
      "description": "CSU Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor (Advanced Manufacturing) Skip to Main Content Cleveland State University Engaged Learning Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor (Advanced Manufacturing) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Business Title Assistant Professor (Advanced Manufacturing) Department Mechanical Engineering Posting Category Faculty Salary Plan Faculty - AAUP Job Summary The Department of Mechanical Engineering in the College of Engineering at Cleveland State University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position starting on August 16, 2027 as part of a multi-hiring initiative in advanced materials and manufacturing. The position is at the rank of Assistant Professor and focuses on advanced manufacturing, materials, and related technologies. The successful candidate will develop an independent, externally funded research program and contribute to the TransDigm Advanced Manufacturing Center’s research enterprise. The position will also support CSU’s commitment to the NSF Engine NEO Smart and is intended to strengthen the University’s competitiveness for NEO Smart competitive grants and other external funding opportunities through research relevant to regional manufacturing needs and in collaboration with industry. The NSF NEO - SMART Engine is Northeast Ohio’s advanced-manufacturing coalition — 70+ partners building on the region’s strength in Advanced Materials and Manufacturing to make more of what America’s factories and defense depend on. The faculty member will also teach undergraduate and graduate courses on-campus, mentor students, and contribute to manufacturing-related courses and microcredentials that prepare a skilled workforce. The position will also support curriculum development for a proposed Industrial and Manufacturing Program within the Mechanical Engineering Department. The faculty member is also expected to participate in service activities through committees, student organization advising, and professional activities outside the University. This position requires teaching on-campus courses. In addition, you may be assigned to teach off campus, evenings, weekends, and via distance learning technology, depending upon student need for the delivery of instructional services. Northeast Ohio is a national hub for advanced manufacturing, integrating innovative technologies such as artificial intelligence (AI) for materials design, automation, and robotics to improve production methods and create new products. Cleveland is home to an ever-growing job market, vibrant and diverse neighborhoods, world-class museums and art institutions, and a thriving culinary scene. From Fortune 500 companies and prestigious healthcare institutions to booming manufacturing companies, Cleveland offers a robust job market for professionals looking to grow in their careers. For more information about Cleveland and Northeast Ohio, see https://discoverthecle.org/ . The Mechanical Engineering Department provides a rigorous education in the principles of mechanical engineering, supplemented by practical hands-on experience and communication skills to transform students into well-rounded and competent engineers. The department offers doctoral, master’s, and an ABET -accredited bachelor’s degree, with currently 385 undergraduate students and 125 graduate students. Our faculty are recipients of prestigious national awards, including 2 NSF CAREER and 2 NIH R01 awards in the last five years. As of Fall 2026, the department’s active research portfolio amounted to an average of $2 million per faculty member in external awards. Current research areas include manufacturing, modeling and simulation of energy systems, turbomachinery rotor dynamics, human-machine systems, robotics, and control systems. For more information about the Department and the Mechanical Engineering Program, please see: https://engineering.csuohio.edu/mce . The university is also well known for its interdisciplinary programs and partnerships with prominent industrial corporations, the Cleveland Clinic, and the NASA Glenn Research Center. CSU aspires to be a national leader in social and economic mobility. We will be a great place to learn and work. CSU is striving to be a nationally recognized and student-focused public research institution that provides accessible, affordable, and Engaged Learning opportunities for all. Minimum Qualifications An undergraduate degree in Mechanical Engineering; and An earned doctoral degree in Mechanical Engineering or a closely related discipline. An appropriate terminal degree must be completed by July 1, 2027 – Persons who are ABD will be hired at the rank of Instructor. Preferred Qualifications BSc degree in Mechanical Engineering from an ABET -accredited program; Track record of scholarly work and sponsored research; Evidence of multidisciplinary research experience including advanced manufacturing, materials processing and development, additive manufacturing, and smart manufacturing Experience teaching mechanical engineering courses at the graduate and/or undergraduate levels; Demonstrate potential for teaching excellence and the highest standards of scholarship and professional activity in the research areas of interest. Date grant, position, or appointment expires (For Funds Available, Temporary, and Waiver of Posting Special Instructions to Applicants Applicant Instructions Applications will only be accepted online at https://hrjobs.csuohio.edu/postings/27426 . Mailed or emailed application materials will not be accepted. Preference will be given to applications received by November 30, 2026. All inquiries about the position should be directed to the Search Committee Chair (Prabaha Sikder, p.sikder@csuohio.edu). List of documents the applicant is required to submit: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Research Statement Contact information for three references – references will be contacted via email and asked to upload a letter of support on your behalf CSU is an urban university with more than 14,000 students located in the heart of Cleveland, OH. According to the Brookings Institution, CSU is No. 18 in the U.S. among public universities that fulfill a critical dual mission: providing upward mobility and conducting impactful research. CSU is the only Ohio university in the top tier of the Brookings list. For additional information about the city of Cleveland, see https://www.thisiscleveland.com/ . Hire is contingent upon the maintenance of existing levels of funding from the State of Ohio. Offer of employment is contingent on satisfactory completion of the University’s verification of credentials (including evidence of a Ph.D.) and other information required by law and/or University policies or practices, including but not limited to a criminal background check. It is the policy of Cleveland State University to provide equal opportunity to all qualified applicants and employees without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, national origin, age, disability, protected veteran, or genetic information. Hiring Range /Pay Rate Advertising Copy Posted Date 10/15/2026 Close Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Review Begins 12/01/2026 Tentative Start Date August 16, 2027 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral CSU Website Other * If you selected 'Public Job Posting\" or \"Other\" please provide source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you require any type of accommodation, should you be invited to campus for further screening? Please contact CSU at (216) 687-3636 if you need accommodation. Yes No * Are you able to perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodation? Yes No Application Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Research Statement Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hrjobs.csuohio.edu/postings/27438": {
      "title": "Assistant / Associate Professor",
      "description": "CSU Applicant Portal | Assistant / Associate Professor Skip to Main Content Cleveland State University Engaged Learning Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant / Associate Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Business Title Assistant / Associate Professor Department Physical Therapy Posting Category Faculty Salary Plan Faculty - AAUP Job Summary The Doctor of Physical Therapy ( DPT ) Program at Cleveland State University is seeking to fill a nine-month, tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor position beginning on August 16, 2027. Rank will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s qualifications and experience. Primary Duties for the position include teaching DPT courses with primary teaching in neurologic physical therapy; being involved in ongoing curriculum development/evaluation; conducting and maintaining research and scholarship; mentoring/advising students; and providing academic, professional, and/or community service. This is an on-campus position. This position requires teaching on-campus courses. In addition, you may be assigned to teach off campus, evenings, weekends, and via distance learning technology, depending upon student need for the delivery of instructional services. Accredited since 1976, the Physical Therapy Department is a part of the College of Health. The DPT Program actively engages students in the educational process and provides an energetic, collegial, and supportive academic environment within the University and the dynamic Cleveland biomedical community. Cleveland State University is an urban campus serving racially, culturally, and economically diverse students. DPT is housed within the College of Health ( COH ), alongside the Departments of Health Sciences and Human Performance, Communication Sciences and Disorders, Occupational Therapy, and Music Therapy; the School of Social Work; and the School of Nursing. Together, the College of Health offers more than 23 undergraduate and graduate programs in health professions, nursing, social work, and related certificate programs. These programs provide students with opportunities for experiential learning, interprofessional practice, and distinct scholarship opportunities. The COH operates two on-site health clinics that provide hands-on training for students while delivering health care services to members of the community. The College of Health is committed to preparing highly qualified researchers and practitioners who can meet the needs of individuals and communities within evolving health care, public health, and wellness environments. CSU aspires to be a national leader in social and economic mobility. We will be a great place to learn and work. CSU is striving to be a nationally recognized and student focused public research institution that provides accessible, affordable, and Engaged Learning opportunities for all. Minimum Qualifications An earned research doctorate (e.g. PhD, EdD, DSc or equivalent) in physical therapy or a related field; Appropriate terminal degree completed by July 1, 2027; Persons who are ABD will be considered for appointment at the rank of Instructor; A physical therapist with eligibility for Ohio PT licensure; A minimum of one year of clinical physical therapy practice experience; Evidence of contemporary expertise in neurologic physical therapy; Evidence of capability to conduct and maintain research and scholarship; Evidence of teaching capability and the capacity to teach core courses across the DPT Program; Strong interpersonal skills, including the ability to collaborate and work on teams. Preferred Qualifications Evidence of excellence in research, including a record of presentations, publications, student and/or colleague mentoring, grant activity, or other scholarly related activities (e.g. journal reviewer); Demonstrated ability to participate in collaborative research and/or clinical practice; APTA board-certified clinical specialist and/or graduate of clinical residency or fellowship training program; Experience in teaching, especially in higher education and/or in physical therapy (e.g. full university course coordination, teaching in an accredited DPT program, graduate level teaching, and other teaching such as continuing education and guest lectures); Experience and ability to teach content related to neurologic physical therapy, as well as a variety of courses across the DPT Program; Evidence of breadth (e.g. variety of settings/practice areas) and/or depth (e.g. years of experience) of clinical practice; Professional, academic, and/or community service and/or leadership. Date grant, position, or appointment expires (For Funds Available, Temporary, and Waiver of Posting Special Instructions to Applicants Applicant Instructions Applications will only be accepted online at https://hrjobs.csuohio.edu/postings/27424 . Mailed or emailed application materials will not be accepted. Preference will be given to applications received by December 1, 2026. All inquiries about the position should be directed to the Search Committee Co-Chairs, Karen McIntyre at k.vitak@csuohio.edu and John Jeziorowski at j.jeziorowski@csuohio.edu. List of documents applicant is required to submit: Cover Letter addressing how you meet the minimum and preferred qualifications – this letter must also include a brief statement of your teaching, research, and service philosophies Curriculum Vitae Contact information for three references (names, addresses, telephone numbers, emails) – references will be contacted by automated email and asked to upload a letter of support on your behalf Optional – License/Certificate* Optional – Unofficial transcript* *Candidates invited to interview will need to submit official transcripts of the highest degree earned, and a copy of Ohio PT licensure or evidence of eligibility (e.g. copy of license in another state) CSU is an urban university with more than 14,000 students located in the heart of Cleveland, OH. According to the Brookings Institution, CSU is No. 18 in the U.S. among public universities that fulfill a critical dual mission: providing upward mobility and conducting impactful research. CSU is the only Ohio university in the top tier of the Brookings list. For additional information about the city of Cleveland, see https://www.thisiscleveland.com/ . Hire is contingent upon the maintenance of existing levels of funding from the State of Ohio. Offer of employment is contingent on satisfactory completion of the University’s verification of credentials (including evidence of a Ph.D.) and other information required by law and/or University policies or practices, including but not limited to a criminal background check. It is the policy of Cleveland State University to provide equal opportunity to all qualified applicants and employees without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, national origin, age, disability, protected veteran, or genetic information. Hiring Range /Pay Rate Commensurate with experience Advertising Copy Posted Date 10/15/2026 Close Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Review Begins 12/02/2026 Tentative Start Date August 16, 2027 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral CSU Website Other * If you selected 'Public Job Posting\" or \"Other\" please provide source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you require any type of accommodation, should you be invited to campus for further screening? Please contact CSU at (216) 687-3636 if you need accommodation. Yes No * Are you able to perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodation? Yes No Application Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents License /Certificate Unofficial Transcripts To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hrjobs.csuohio.edu/postings/27437": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "CSU Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Cleveland State University Engaged Learning Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Business Title Assistant Professor Department Mechanical Engineering Posting Category Faculty Salary Plan Faculty - AAUP Job Summary The Department of Mechanical Engineering at Cleveland State University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor to start on August 16, 2027 as part of a multiple hiring initiative for the department. Expertise is sought in the broad areas of Biomechanics, Human Motion and Control, Human-Machine Systems, and Rehabilitation. The position will support the research activities of the CSU Center for Human-Machine Systems and the planned Biomedical Discovery Complex. Candidates are expected to develop and grow an externally funded research program and teach courses to meet the needs of the undergraduate and graduate curriculum. The candidate is also expected to participate in service activities through committees, student organization advising and professional activities outside the University. This position requires teaching on-campus courses. In addition, you may be assigned to teach off campus, evenings, weekends, and via distance learning technology, depending upon student need for the delivery of instructional services. The university is well-known for its interdisciplinary programs, enjoying partnerships with prominent industrial corporations, the Cleveland Clinic and the NASA Glenn Research Center. The Mechanical Engineering Department provides a rigorous education in the principles of mechanical engineering, supplemented by practical hands-on experience and communication skills to transform students into well-rounded and competent engineers. The department offers PhDl, master’s and an ABET -accredited bachelor’s degree, with currently 385 undergraduate students and 125 graduate students. Our faculty are recipients of prestigious national awards, including 2 NSF CAREER and 2 NIH R01 awards in the last five years. As of Fall 2026, the department’s active research portfolio amounted to an average of $2 million per faculty member in external awards. Current areas of research include manufacturing, modeling and simulation of energy systems, turbomachinery rotordynamics, human-machine systems, robotics, and control systems. Cleveland is home to an ever-growing job market, vibrant and diverse neighborhoods, world-class museums and art institutions, and a thriving culinary scene. From Fortune 500 companies and prestigious healthcare institutions to booming manufacturing companies, Cleveland offers a robust job market for professionals looking to grow in their careers. For more information about Cleveland and Northeast Ohio, see https://discoverthecle.org/. CSU aspires to be a national leader in social and economic mobility. We will be a great place to learn and work. CSU is striving to be a nationally recognized and student focused public research institution that provides accessible, affordable, and Engaged Learning opportunities for all. Minimum Qualifications An undergraduate degree in Mechanical Engineering; and An earned doctoral degree in Mechanical Engineering or a closely related discipline. Appropriate terminal degree completed by July 1, 2027. Persons who are ABD will be hired at the rank of Instructor. Preferred Qualifications Potential for excellence in research mentoring and fostering high standards of scholarship in students; Teaching experience and potential for teaching effectiveness in mechanical engineering; Evidence of research experience including biomechanics, human-machine systems or rehabilitation; Track record of scholarly work and relevant professional activity, and potential to establish an independent, externally funded research program. Date grant, position, or appointment expires (For Funds Available, Temporary, and Waiver of Posting Special Instructions to Applicants Applicant Instructions Applications will only be accepted online at https://hrjobs.csuohio.edu/postings/27390 . Mailed or emailed application materials will not be accepted. Preference will be given to applications received by December 11, 2026. All inquiries about the position should be directed to the Search Committee Chair, Prof. Hanz Richter, h.richter@csuohio.edu. List of documents applicant is required to submit: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Research Plan Contact information for three references – references will be contacted via email and asked to upload a letter of support on your behalf CSU is an urban university with more than 14,000 students located in the heart of Cleveland, OH. According to the Brookings Institution, CSU is No. 18 in the U.S. among public universities that fulfill a critical dual mission: providing upward mobility and conducting impactful research. CSU is the only Ohio university in the top tier of the Brookings list. For additional information about the city of Cleveland, see https://www.thisiscleveland.com/ . Hire is contingent upon the maintenance of existing levels of funding from the State of Ohio. Offer of employment is contingent on satisfactory completion of the University’s verification of credentials (including evidence of a Ph.D.) and other information required by law and/or University policies or practices, including but not limited to a criminal background check. It is the policy of Cleveland State University to provide equal opportunity to all qualified applicants and employees without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, national origin, age, disability, protected veteran, or genetic information. Hiring Range /Pay Rate Commensurate with experience Advertising Copy Posted Date 10/15/2026 Close Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Review Begins 12/14/2026 Tentative Start Date August 16, 2027 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral CSU Website Other * If you selected 'Public Job Posting\" or \"Other\" please provide source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you require any type of accommodation, should you be invited to campus for further screening? Please contact CSU at (216) 687-3636 if you need accommodation. Yes No * Are you able to perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodation? Yes No Application Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Research Plan Teaching Statement Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
