    "https://hrjobs.csuohio.edu/postings/27433": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "CSU Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Cleveland State University Engaged Learning Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Business Title Assistant Professor Department Maxine Goodman Levin School of Urban Affairs Posting Category Faculty Salary Plan Faculty - AAUP Job Summary The Maxine Goodman Levin School of Urban Affairs seeks adynamic faculty member at the rank of Assistant Professor. The start date is August 16, 2027. Successful candidates will contribute fully to the Levin School through teaching, research, and service. While we will consider all areas of expertise related to urban planning and/or urban affairs, we are particularly interested in candidates who can bolster our research and teaching portfolio in urban real estate development and finance; community development; environmental planning and policy; and/or applications of data science and/or AI in urban affairs research and practice. We especially encourage candidates who have experience and interest in engaged teaching and research. This position requires teaching on-campus courses. In addition, you may be assigned to teach off campus, evenings, weekends, and via distance learning technology, depending upon student need for the delivery of instructional services. The Levin School of Urban Affairs is ranked among the top urban affairs schools in the nation, including #3 in urban policy and #10 in local government. The school offers four master’s degrees including the fully accredited Master of Public Administration and Master of Urban Planning and Development, along with a Master of Nonprofit Administration and Master of Science in Urban Studies. We also have a Ph.D. in Urban Studies & Public Affairs and six undergraduate majors in community planning, environmental studies, nonprofit administration, organizational leadership, public policy and management, and public safety management. The Levin School is housed within the Levin College of Public Affairs and Education, which also includes the School of Education & Counseling, the School of Communication, and the Department of Criminology and Sociology. The Levin College houses a number of research and career enhancement centers such as the Center for Economic Development, the Energy Policy Center, and the Center for Public and Nonprofit Management. This dynamic environment provides opportunities for interdisciplinary, applied, and engaged research and teaching. CSU aspires to be a national leader in social and economic mobility. We will be a great place to learn and work. CSU is striving to be a nationally recognized and student focused public research institution that provides accessible, affordable, and Engaged Learning opportunities for all. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Urban Planning, Public Administration, Public Policy, Urban Studies, or a closely related field completed by July 1, 2027 (persons who are ABD will be hired at the rank of Instructor); Research agenda focused on urban affairs or related field; Excellent communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Expertise in one or more of the following areas: economic development, urban real estate development and finance; community development; environmental planning and policy; and/or applications of data science and/or AI in urban affairs research and/or practice; Willing and able to apply an interdisciplinary approach to research; Commitment to community engagement in both teaching and research; Teaching experience; Experience teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses in urban planning; Experience with online, remote, and/or hybrid teaching formats; Openness to interdisciplinary research. Date grant, position, or appointment expires (For Funds Available, Temporary, and Waiver of Posting Special Instructions to Applicants Applicant Instructions Applications will only be accepted online at https://hrjobs.csuohio.edu/postings/27380 . Mailed or emailed application materials will not be accepted. Preference will be given to applications received by November 15, 2026. All inquiries about the position should be directed to the Search Committee Chair, Joanna Ganning (j.ganning@csuohio.edu). List of documents applicant is required to submit: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching statement, including a summary of course evaluations (if available) Research statement Contact information for three references – references will be contacted via email and asked to upload a letter of support on your behalf CSU is an urban university with more than 14,000 students located in the heart of Cleveland, OH. According to the Brookings Institution, CSU is No. 18 in the U.S. among public universities that fulfill a critical dual mission: providing upward mobility and conducting impactful research. CSU is the only Ohio university in the top tier of the Brookings list. For additional information about the city of Cleveland, see https://www.thisiscleveland.com/ . Hire is contingent upon the maintenance of existing levels of funding from the State of Ohio. Offer of employment is contingent on satisfactory completion of the University’s verification of credentials (including evidence of a Ph.D.) and other information required by law and/or University policies or practices, including but not limited to a criminal background check. It is the policy of Cleveland State University to provide equal opportunity to all qualified applicants and employees without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, national origin, age, disability, protected veteran, or genetic information. Hiring Range /Pay Rate Advertising Copy Posted Date 10/15/2026 Close Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Review Begins 11/15/2026 Tentative Start Date August 16, 2027 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral CSU Website Other * If you selected 'Public Job Posting\" or \"Other\" please provide source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you require any type of accommodation, should you be invited to campus for further screening? Please contact CSU at (216) 687-3636 if you need accommodation. Yes No * Are you able to perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodation? Yes No Application Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Research Statement Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hrjobs.csuohio.edu/postings/27431": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "CSU Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Cleveland State University Engaged Learning Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Business Title Assistant Professor Department Civil Engineering Posting Category Faculty Salary Plan Faculty - AAUP Job Summary The Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering ( CVE ) at Cleveland State University ( CSU ) invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Environmental Engineering at the rank of Assistant Professor, with an anticipated start date of August 16, 2027. The successful candidate will be expected to: (1) Teach undergraduate and graduate environmental engineering courses; (2) Establish and sustain an innovative, externally funded research program addressing critical environmental challenges; and (3) Mentor and supervise student research and contribute services to the Department, College, University, and professional societies. This position requires teaching on-campus courses. In addition, you may be assigned to teach off campus, evenings, weekends, and via distance learning technology, depending upon student need for the delivery of instructional services. To complement its existing strengths in environmental engineering, the Department seeks candidates with a global perspective and a commitment to addressing critical environmental challenges through the integration of engineering and science. Preference will be given to applicants whose research demonstrates significant societal impact. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, innovative water quality management in watersheds and large water bodies, emerging contaminants and environmental health, sustainable and smart urban infrastructure, and greenhouse gas mitigation to improve air quality and enhance climate resilience. Opportunities for engagement in the greater Cleveland metro area include the Cleveland Metroparks, which has a significant number of ongoing small and large planning and design projects, and the Cleveland Water Alliance, which is engaged in two NSF Engines and manages the world’s largest digitally connected freshwater testbed. CSU aspires to be a national leader in social and economic mobility. We will be a great place to learn and work. CSU is striving to be a nationally recognized and student focused public research institution that provides accessible, affordable, and Engaged Learning opportunities for all. Minimum Qualifications Undergraduate degree in civil (or environmental) engineering or closely related fields; Earned doctoral degree in civil (or environmental) engineering or closely related fields by the appointment start date – Persons who are ABD will be hired at the rank of Instructor; Research experience or professional practices in environmental engineering; and Record of peer-reviewed publications. Preferred Qualifications Postdoctoral experience; Professional Engineer (PE) registration; Research experience in sustainable and smart urban infrastructures; water quality management of large water bodies such as the Great Lakes; or greenhouse gas mitigation for climate resilience; Record of externally funded research as a PI or co-PI; Demonstrated excellence in teaching evidenced by student evaluations; and Demonstrated commitment to student mentorship and research supervision. Date grant, position, or appointment expires (For Funds Available, Temporary, and Waiver of Posting Special Instructions to Applicants Applicant Instructions Applications will only be accepted online at https://hrjobs.csuohio.edu/postings/27370 . Mailed or emailed application materials will not be accepted. Preference will be given to applications received by December 1, 2026, and review will continue until the position is filled. All inquiries about the position should be directed to the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Ungtae Kim at u.kim@csuohio.edu. Applicants must submit the following materials through the CSU online application system: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae detailing educational background, professional experience, teaching record, list of peer-reviewed publications, and list of externally funded research Teaching Statement describing teaching philosophy, instructional experience, pedagogical training, and a summary of student evaluations (maximum 2 pages) Research Statement outlining current and future research interests and development plan (maximum 2 pages). Please do not attach the copies of journal articles Unofficial Transcripts for all earned and pursuing degrees Contact Information for Three References* (name, institutional affiliation, mailing address, email address, and telephone number) to be entered directly into the CSU online application system *References will not be contacted until the later stages of the search process. CSU is an urban university with more than 14,000 students located in the heart of Cleveland, OH. According to the Brookings Institution, CSU is No. 18 in the U.S. among public universities that fulfill a critical dual mission: providing upward mobility and conducting impactful research. CSU is the only Ohio university in the top tier of the Brookings list. For additional information about the city of Cleveland, see https://www.thisiscleveland.com/ . Hire is contingent upon the maintenance of existing levels of funding from the State of Ohio. Offer of employment is contingent on satisfactory completion of the University’s verification of credentials (including evidence of a Ph.D.) and other information required by law and/or University policies or practices, including but not limited to a criminal background check. It is the policy of Cleveland State University to provide equal opportunity to all qualified applicants and employees without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, national origin, age, disability, protected veteran, or genetic information. Hiring Range /Pay Rate Competitive Salary Advertising Copy Posted Date 10/15/2026 Close Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Review Begins 12/01/2026 Tentative Start Date August 16, 2027 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral CSU Website Other * If you selected 'Public Job Posting\" or \"Other\" please provide source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you require any type of accommodation, should you be invited to campus for further screening? Please contact CSU at (216) 687-3636 if you need accommodation. Yes No * Are you able to perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodation? Yes No Application Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement Research Statement Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://hrjobs.csuohio.edu/postings/27393": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor",
      "description": "CSU Applicant Portal | Assistant or Associate Professor Skip to Main Content Cleveland State University Engaged Learning Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant or Associate Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Business Title Assistant or Associate Professor Department Health Science and Human Performance Posting Category Faculty Salary Plan Faculty - AAUP Job Summary The Department of Health Sciences and Human Performance ( HSHP ) at Cleveland State University invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor position beginning on January 2, 2027. Rank will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s qualifications and experience. Primary responsibilities include establishing and maintaining a robust, active research agenda; pursuing and securing external research funding; and teaching across the undergraduate and graduate curricula. The successful candidate will teach core and elective courses in the Master of Public Health ( MPH ) program and may also teach core HSHP courses, depending on departmental needs and the candidate’s expertise. Potential course areas include wellness, nutrition, population health, health services research, and health education. The position will also include oversight of the MPH Capstone experience. Additional responsibilities include mentoring and advising students in research methods, supervising student research projects, and contributing to academic, professional, and institutional service. This is an on-campus position, with the possibility of a supplemental summer contract based on operational needs. The Department of Health Sciences and Human Performance ( HSHP ) offers innovative undergraduate and graduate programs, including a Commission on Accreditation of Allied Health Education Programs ( CAAHEP )-accredited Bachelor of Science in Exercise Science and a Bachelor of Science in Health Sciences with multiple career-focused tracks. The department also participates in an accredited Master of Public Health ( MPH ) program offered through a four-institution consortium. HSHP is housed within the College of Health ( COH ), alongside the Departments of Physical Therapy, Communication Sciences and Disorders, Occupational Therapy, and Music Therapy; the School of Social Work; and the School of Nursing. Together, the College of Health offers more than 23 undergraduate and graduate programs in health professions, nursing, social work, and related certificate programs. These programs provide students with opportunities for experiential learning, interprofessional practice, and distinct scholarship opportunities. The COH operates two on-site health clinics that provide hands-on training for students while delivering health care services to members of the community. The College of Health is committed to preparing highly qualified researchers and practitioners who can meet the needs of individuals and communities within evolving health care, public health, and wellness environments. CSU aspires to be a national leader in social and economic mobility. We will be a great place to learn and work. CSU is striving to be a nationally recognized and student focused public research institution that provides accessible, affordable, and Engaged Learning opportunities for all. Minimum Qualifications Earned Doctorate in Public Health (e.g., DrPH, PhD), Health Sciences, Health Education, Exercise Science, Nutrition, or a closely related field, obtained by date of hire, Earned Master of Public Health ( MPH ) degree by the date of hire, Evidence of an active research agenda with a clear trajectory for conducting a sustained program of research at CSU and in relevant community or professional settings, disseminating scholarly findings, and pursuing external grant funding, Experience mentoring and supervising undergraduate or graduate students in research projects, theses, independent studies, and/or capstone projects, Experience or demonstrated potential to teach a range of core courses in the MPH program, graduate-level public health courses, and other courses within the HSHP Department, including, but not limited to, exercise science, nutrition, general health science, and health education, Evidence of strong interpersonal and communication skills, including the ability to collaborate effectively in research teams and mentor students. Preferred Qualifications Research experience in a public health specialty area and/or a demonstrated record of securing external research funding, including federal, state, foundation or other competitive grants, Experience teaching in higher education, in both in-person and online formats, including full-course coordination, teaching in an accredited program, and graduate-level instruction. Teaching experience in grant writing, research methods, program evaluation, data analytics, and prevention science, Evidence of peer-reviewed publications, national presentations, and active involvement in relevant professional public health or health science organizations, Experience integrating technology, biostatistics, AI, data analytics, or health informatics into research and instruction, Familiarity with curriculum development, program evaluation, and assessment aligned with higher education and institutional accreditation standards, Certified Public Health ( CPH ) credential preferred. Date grant, position, or appointment expires (For Funds Available, Temporary, and Waiver of Posting Special Instructions to Applicants Applicant Instructions Applications will only be accepted online at https://hrjobs.csuohio.edu/postings/27306 . Mailed or emailed application materials will not be accepted. Preference will be given to applications received by November 1, 2026. All inquiries about the position should be directed to the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Andrew Lammers at a.lammers13@csuohio.edu. List of documents applicant is required to submit: Cover letter addressing how you meet the minimum and preferred qualifications – this letter must include a statement detailing your research agenda (including funding plans), teaching philosophy, and approach to student mentorship. Curriculum vitae. Evidence of teaching and research effectiveness – applicants should include evidence of effective teaching/supervision (e.g., teaching evaluations) and examples of scholarly work (e.g., recent publications, writing samples, or grant abstracts). Unofficial transcripts* of a) MPH degree and b) highest degree earned. Contact information for three references (names, addresses, telephone numbers, emails) – references will be contacted by automated email to upload a letter of support on your behalf. OPTIONAL – Applicants may also submit relevant professional licenses or certifications. *Candidates invited to interview will need to submit official transcripts of the highest degree earned and the MPH and a copy of relevant certifications/licensure at the time of campus interview acceptance. CSU is an urban university with more than 14,000 students located in the heart of Cleveland, OH. According to the Brookings Institution, CSU is No. 18 in the U.S. among public universities that fulfill a critical dual mission: providing upward mobility and conducting impactful research. CSU is the only university in Ohio in the top tier of the Brookings list. For additional information about the city of Cleveland, see https://www.thisiscleveland.com/ . Hiring is contingent upon the maintenance of existing levels of funding from the State of Ohio. Offer of employment is contingent on satisfactory completion of the University’s verification of credentials and other information required by law and/or University policies or practices, including but not limited to a criminal background check. It is the policy of Cleveland State University to provide equal opportunity to all qualified applicants and employees without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, national origin, age, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. CSU aspires to be a national leader in social and economic mobility. We are a great place to learn and work. CSU is striving to be a nationally recognized and student-focused public research institution that provides accessible, affordable, and Engaged Learning opportunities for all. Hiring Range /Pay Rate competitive salary Advertising Copy Posted Date 10/07/2026 Close Date/Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Review Begins 11/02/2026 Tentative Start Date January 2, 2027 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral CSU Website Other * If you selected 'Public Job Posting\" or \"Other\" please provide source. (Open Ended Question) * Do you require any type of accommodation, should you be invited to campus for further screening? Please contact CSU at (216) 687-3636 if you need accommodation. Yes No * Are you able to perform the essential functions of this position with or without reasonable accommodation? Yes No Application Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Evidence of Teaching Experience (e.g. Course Evals, etc.) Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents License /Certificate To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
